Default EC2 Configuration modules
================================
This module provisions EC2 instances with default configurations. It is designed to be reusable across different environments, allowing for consistent and efficient deployment of EC2 resources.
Module Structure
----------------
The module is organized as follows:
```
ec2/
├─ main.tf               # Main configuration file for EC2 instances
├─ variables.tf          # Input variable definitions
├─ outputs.tf            # Output definitions
├─ user_data.sh          # User data script for instance initialization
└─ README.AD             # Module documentation
```
Input Variables 
----------------
The module accepts the following input variables:
- `instance_type` (string): The type of EC2 instance to launch. Default is "t2.micro".
- `ami_id` (string): The AMI ID to use for the EC2 instance
- `key_name` (string): The name of the key pair to use for SSH access.
- `subnet_id` (string): The ID of the subnet where the instance will be launched.
- `security_group_ids` (list): A list of security group IDs to associate with the instance.
- 'servertype' (string): The type of server (e.g., "web", "db").
- `tags` (map): A map of tags to assign to the instance.
Output Variables
----------------
The module provides the following output variables:
- `instance_id` (string): The ID of the created EC2 instance.
- `public_ip` (string): The public IP address of the EC2 instance.
- `private_ip` (string): The private IP address of the EC2 instance.
Usage
-----
To use this module, include it in your Terraform configuration as follows:
```hcl
module "ec2_instance" {
  source              = "../modules/ec2"
  instance_type       = "t2.micro"
  ami_id              = "ami-0abcdef1234567890"
  key_name            = "my-key-pair"
  subnet_id           = "subnet-0123456789abcdef0"
  security_group_ids  = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]
  tags = {
    Name = "MyEC2Instance"
    Environment = "Non-Prod"
  }
}